From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tinnci <23432137+Tinnci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt8183: Handle empty AFE MCU IRQ status
 as spurious

On a google,krane MT8183 system running a full-duplex PipeWire path,
mt8183_afe_irq_handler() can be entered with regmap_read() succeeding but
with no low AFE_IRQ_STATUS_BITS set in AFE_IRQ_MCU_STATUS.

The observed samples have changing high bits, mcu_en=0xffff, and no active
low status bit. Returning IRQ_NONE logs repeated "irq status err" messages
for an interrupt that appears to be late/spurious rather than a failed
register read. Active PCM streams continue running.

Keep the regmap_read() failure path as an error, but treat an empty MCU-owned
status as a handled spurious interrupt and rate-limit it at debug level.

This is a local RFC test patch. Replace this header and add a real
Signed-off-by before sending upstream.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt8183/mt8183-afe-pcm.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8183/mt8183-afe-pcm.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8183/mt8183-afe-pcm.c
index 8a99f8eaf0e8..86106dbe39f3 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8183/mt8183-afe-pcm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt8183/mt8183-afe-pcm.c
@@ -636,14 +636,21 @@ static irqreturn_t mt8183_afe_irq_handler(int irq_id, void *dev)
 	/* only care IRQ which is sent to MCU */
 	status_mcu = status & mcu_en & AFE_IRQ_STATUS_BITS;
 
-	if (ret || status_mcu == 0) {
-		dev_err(afe->dev, "%s(), irq status err, ret %d, status 0x%x, mcu_en 0x%x\n",
-			__func__, ret, status, mcu_en);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(afe->dev, "%s(), irq status err, ret %d, mcu_en 0x%x\n",
+			__func__, ret, mcu_en);
 
 		irq_ret = IRQ_NONE;
 		goto err_irq;
 	}
 
+	if (!status_mcu) {
+		dev_dbg_ratelimited(afe->dev,
+				    "%s(), spurious irq, status 0x%x, mcu_en 0x%x\n",
+				    __func__, status, mcu_en);
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < MT8183_MEMIF_NUM; i++) {
 		struct mtk_base_afe_memif *memif = &afe->memif[i];
 
